# Keeping the build context small is the smaller reason for this file. The bigger
# one is that a few of these would be actively harmful inside the image.

# Secrets. `.env.local` holds the real AUTH_SECRET, and COPY . . would bake it into
# a layer — where it stays even if a later step deletes it.
.env*
!.env.example

# The dev database, and the e2e one. Copying either would ship real data and then
# be shadowed by the /data volume anyway.
data

# Build output. Stale artifacts from a host build would be copied in and then
# partially overwritten, which is worse than starting clean.
.next
out
build
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Installed on the host, for the host's platform. The native addons in here
# (@libsql/darwin-arm64, sharp) are the wrong architecture for the image.
node_modules

# Nothing the build needs.
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
e2e/.auth
.local-storage
.DS_Store
*.log

# Docs and tooling that don't affect the build.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
DEVELOPMENT.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
